    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this exists",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-09-30 over 300 `main`-into-branch merges on `origin/claude/*`\n(bean `y7b3`, issue #1707): **235 conflicted, and 147 (63 %) conflicted only on\ngenerated files. Every one of those resolves the same way — take the base's\ncopy, regenerate — and each cost an agent a round and the PR another CI run. Owner, 2026-10-01: *\"1 + new skills/tools for each common churn/conflict\npattern\"*, and *\"put in merge process bpmn\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean y7b3",
        "#1707",
        "2026-09-30",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30",
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The three rules that make it safe",
      "prov:value": "### Why rule 3 is a rule and not a footnote"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why rule 3 is a rule and not a footnote",
      "prov:value": "This is the same shape as `1xhc` one level out: a stale instrument and a\ncorrect one are indistinguishable from their output, and the stale one here\nreads as *more* work rather than less, so nothing about the result looks\nwrong."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why rule 3 is a rule and not a footnote",
      "prov:value": "## A merge round — run each check ONCE (owner ruling, 2026-10-05)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "When every conflict is generated — the trimmed round",
      "prov:value": "**Targeted checks, and only these:**\n   - `skill:register:check` and `kg:detangle:check` — the two reds a\n     generated-only merge actually hit in CI;\n   - `subgraph:jsonld:check` — a merge or edit that changes a skill also\n     changes its payload hash; `skill:register` does not run\n     `subgraph:jsonld`, so run the writer (`bun run cat subgraph:jsonld`) when the\n     check is red. Measured on #2139 itself: CI's `gen-slice-sqlite` test\n     failed on three edited skills whose payloads the published tree did not\n     hold;\n   - `check:declared-paths` (never with `--update` here) and\n     `check:process-index`;\n   - `bun run typecheck`, and `bun run cat lint` at **0 errors**;\n   - **the deletion audit** —\n     `git diff --name-status --diff-filter=D HEAD^1 HEAD -- '*/test/results/*'`\n     must list only files `main` itself deleted. A gitignored-but-tracked file\n     is dropped by a merge silently, local checks stay green because the\n     writer recreated it on disk, and CI's fresh checkout fails (bean `8j9e`). `merge:main` now refuses such a drop itself (§\"When one side deleted\n     the file\"); after a hand merge, restore each one main still tracks with\n     `git checkout HEAD^2 -- <path>`;\n   - **submodule pins equal to `main`'s** —\n     `git ls-tree HEAD bootstrap bootstrap-tools` against\n     `git ls-tree origin/main bootstrap bootstrap-tools`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8j9e",
        "#2139"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "When it is NOT generated-only — keep the full local run",
      "prov:value": "The targeted list above is chosen for a merge\nthat changed only artefacts with one right answer. A semantic conflict — #2043\nimporting a module #2112 had moved, in\n[`merge-queue`](merge-queue.md) §\"A train admits only members that STACK\ncleanly\" — is exactly what that list cannot see.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2043",
        "#2112"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Four things a round needs to know",
      "prov:value": "Merging now buys a second round the moment it lands — on train\n  `merge-train-2026-10-04a`, #2112 landing mid-round re-conflicted the train\n  and cost another 12-minute regen plus a semantic conflict\n  ([`merge-queue`](merge-queue.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2112",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pattern is not always the answer — ask what the file's record is",
      "prov:value": "- **bean `in5a`** — a declared pattern settles a file whose content is a\n  function of the TREE, and settles nothing about one whose content is a\n  function of the machine that built it. There, take-base is a loop: take\n  either side, regenerate, and the value is whatever this container sees. - **this section** — the content *is* tree-determined, the pattern *does*\n  resolve it, and the path still conflicts on every merge.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean in5a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pattern is not always the answer — ask what the file's record is",
      "prov:value": "The worked example is bean `tqjj`, and the measurement is what makes it a rule\nrather than a preference. `**/test/results/lsi/**` and\n`**/test/results/tool-runs/**` have been declared under `derived-results` all\nalong, and `cat-harness/docs/lsi/**` under `glossary`. On 2026-10-04 those three\npaths were still blocking **seven open pull requests each**, 317-319 of the last\n400 commits on `main` touching them. Regenerating `skills.lsi.json` on an\nunchanged tree gave a **byte-identical** file, so `in5a` did not apply; but\nappending one sentence to one of 229 skill files rewrote the `fingerprint`,\n**9 of 12** `dimensions` entries and **166 of 229** `neighbours` entries. An\nSVD rotation is globally sensitive, so the convergent resolution is a rewrite\nof 94 % of the file — and nothing on `main` judged those bytes: corrupting the\nsidecar's `fingerprint` left `lsi:skills:check` at exit 0 (`.gitattributes`,\nbean `eqxp`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tqjj",
        "bean eqxp",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pattern is not always the answer — ask what the file's record is",
      "prov:value": "Taking a page off its store and leaving it\ncommitted can make it *worse*: once `lsi:viz` had no sidecar in the checkout it\nread `qa-reports` at `main`, which resolves to the **latest published entry**,\nso the committed page would have gone stale whenever anyone else pushed — a\nvalue depending on when the gate ran rather than on the tree. **`in5a`'s loop,\narriving over the network. Whatever stays committed must be computed from the\ntree, deliberately and not by luck."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A pattern is not always the answer — ask what the file's record is",
      "prov:value": "`.gitattributes` reached the same conclusion from the `-merge` side and states\nit plainly: *\"Removing these conflicts, rather than tidying them, needs the\nfiles off `main` altogether.\"* Two things make that safe rather than merely\ntidy, and both are checks, not care: every reader must already cope with the\nfile's absence (bean `oq1j` for the LSI readers), and something must still\nPRODUCE it where its record lives — `qa:refresh` decides that **per writer**,\nso a family can be removed on its own instead of all 1,186 at once.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean oq1j"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When one side deleted the file",
      "prov:value": "The retired `qa:resolve-conflicts` did the same for the\nsidecars it was delegated (#1854, bean `7mwa`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7mwa",
        "#1854"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When one side deleted the file",
      "prov:value": "**Taking a deletion is the ONLY way a merge may drop a path, and\n`merge-base.ts` checks this before every merge commit** (beans `vsv7`,\n`8j9e`). `git add -A` is not what removes such a file, though. It stages a\nrewrite of a file that is still tracked; it only fails to restore one that\nsomething has already removed from the index. On #1898 (`edf52fcf6`) that was\na `git rm` from `takeBase`. `qa:resolve-conflicts`, retired since, claimed\nevery conflicted path under a declared `qa` directory, detangle sidecars\nincluded, and had already resolved three of them. The pre-`vsv7` `takeBase` then read \"no\nstages\" as \"the base deleted it\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vsv7",
        "bean 8j9e",
        "#1898"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The patterns",
      "prov:value": "Counts are conflicted files in the 2026-09-30 measurement.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`kg-qa-manifest` — take the base, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "Not in the first measurement's top list; found when a replay of 40 real\nmerges refused one merge on these files alone."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`qa-results` — take the base, regenerate (292)",
      "prov:value": "They carried `updated_at` until #1714; they still change whenever\nany finding does.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1714"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`derived-results` — take the base, regenerate (142)",
      "prov:value": "The **kg-qa** sidecars joined in bean `7mwa`. They were the `kg-qa-sidecar`\npattern (53 conflicts in the measurement), delegated to `qa:resolve-conflicts`\nbecause a sidecar could carry an attestation no generator reproduces. The\nattestations moved to `test/attestations/` (bean `2gst`), which no pattern\nnames and a merge therefore refuses, and cat-harness and the content core\n(https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant-core) stopped committing `test/results/`. So the command and the pattern were\nretired, and a branch still carrying a sidecar takes the base's side.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7mwa",
        "bean 2gst"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`prov-qaqc` — take the base, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "**Added 2026-10-03, and the occasion is the reason. The runner refused #1892\nwith `docs/prov-qaqc/index.md` as the SINGLE unclassified path among **32**\nresolved by pattern. One file nobody authors, blocking a merge nobody can\nusefully resolve by hand — which is this catalogue's whole purpose, missing one\nentry.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1892",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`glossary` — take the base, regenerate (207)",
      "prov:value": "The **LSI page** still conflicts, but much less often since bean `tqjj`: its\nper-index detail — the half a one-sentence skill edit moved — is added by the\ndocs-site build rather than committed, and what is left is a function of the\ntree.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tqjj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`translated-glossary` — take the base, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "Not in the first measurement; found\n2026-10-01 when a `merge:main` on #1754 refused on all five.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1754",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`viewer-pages` — take the base, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "`docs/fsh-guts/index.md` USED to be here: any PR that archived an upload\nrewrote it, so two such PRs always collided (#1766, 2026-10-03). It is no\nlonger committed at all. It is derived from `fsh-guts/`, which is kept on a\nbranch, so it is built at publish by `derive:publish` (bean `0b8c`, #2230),\nand a merge cannot meet it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0b8c",
        "#1766",
        "#2230",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`viewer-namespace` — take the base, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "Same false positive as above: its `uploads/` pages render\nuploads rather than being them (#1775).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1775"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`skos-glossary-export` — take the base, regenerate (54)",
      "prov:value": "Bean `8rff` measured **54** pair-path hits across 32 open PRs — every\ninstance's export restamps whenever any declared role, skill or term moves, so\ntwo PRs that touch unrelated skills still collide here.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8rff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`skos-glossary-export` — take the base, regenerate (54)",
      "prov:value": "`glossary-ledger.json` carries forward: `glossary-export.ts` reads the prior\nledger and preserves a concept's earlier names as `skos:hiddenLabel` (#1168\nB10b), so taking one side would drop a term's history.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1168"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs-pages` — take the base, regenerate (17)",
      "prov:value": "Bean `8c6v`: **none** of the 17 was named by a pattern, so `classify()`\nreturned `refuse / — none —` and the merge handed back for hand-editing the\nfiles that forbid it. `docs/process/publication-workflow.md` was one of the **2**\nrefusals on #1888 after **53** of its 55 conflicts had resolved by pattern —\none undeclared family holding up a 53-file resolution is the all-or-nothing\nrule working as designed, and the gap it exposed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8c6v",
        "#1888"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs-pages` — take the base, regenerate (17)",
      "prov:value": "**That test must read the front matter, not the file**, and it earned the\ndistinction immediately. Its first cut tested the whole file for the marker\nand the very next merge of `main` turned up an 18th subject: the generated\nbody of **this skill**, `docs/reference/skill-instructions/merge-conflict-patterns.md`,\nwhich quotes the marker in the code fence three paragraphs above. A detector\nthat reads a quotation as a declaration finds its own documentation — *\"a\ndocblock that documents a tag necessarily contains the tag\"*, from\n[`audit-coverage`](../../../skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md). That page's own front\nmatter names `gen-skill-docs.ts`, and `skill-instructions` is declared before\n`docs-pages`, so the first match already gives it the right owner. A test pins\nall three facts."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs-pages` — take the base, regenerate (17)",
      "prov:value": "`cat-harness/docs/source/process-publication-workflow/every-workflow-in-the-repo.md`\nis the hand-written INPUT for `docs/process/publication-workflow.md`; on #1888 both\nsides had only *added* rows to it, but a union of additions is a property of\nthat instance and not of the path, so the next conflict there could be a\ncontested edit.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1888"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`subgraph-index` and `subgraph-payload` — owned tree, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "Any skill edit rewrites an index and moves a payload, so until #2176\n(2026-10-05) every merge of `main` into a PR that edited a skill was refused,\nand a person finished it by hand: `checkout --theirs`, then `subgraph:jsonld`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2176",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`subgraph-index` and `subgraph-payload` — owned tree, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "**Both #2145 checkpoints still hold, and they are why this works.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2145"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`navbar-rail-data` — owned tree, regenerate",
      "prov:value": "`seed:ready` reads the same declaration: deleting or renaming an `owned-tree`\npath is not a move of the layer, because a regen renames it anyway (owner,\n2026-10-06).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`readme-generated-regions` — hunk by hunk (209)",
      "prov:value": "The file-count churn\n(`beans/README.md`, 76 alone) is resolved here rather than by changing what\nthe README shows — the owner kept the exact counts (#1707).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1707"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`standalone-baseline` — take the base, regenerate NOTHING",
      "prov:value": "`cat-harness-tools/scripts/standalone-baseline.json`, `check:standalone`'s list of\naccepted standalone failures (bean `ho66`, #1977). Not measured by replay: the file was new when\nthe pattern was added, so there was no merge history to count.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ho66",
        "#1977"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`beans` — refused, by declaration (44)",
      "prov:value": "The second is `beans:claim`'s **normal path**, not an edge case: it pushes the\nclaim to the default branch so a sibling sees it before your PR exists (bean\n`35nj`), and your branch then edits the same bean to finish it. Bean `24fa`\nmeasured it, and the refusal text used to assert the first cause for both —\nsending an agent to hunt a sibling that does not exist.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 35nj",
        "bean 24fa"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "`artefact-verification` — refused, by declaration",
      "prov:value": "**This is the entry that exists to stop a sweep, not to resolve\none** — and the one most likely to be globed by mistake, because it reads like a\ngenerated sidecar (under `scripts/`, a `.json`, its key set derived from\n`package.json`) and because it is the only path that refused on **two** open PRs\nat once (#1958, #1955, swept 2026-10-03).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1958",
        "#1955",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`artefact-verification` — refused, by declaration",
      "prov:value": "**The falsifier is recorded** (bean `mjl3`): if a `--write` is ever added that\ncomposes the derived key set and carries existing reasons forward, the file\nbecomes regenerable and this entry becomes `take-base`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mjl3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "In CI — opt in with the `merge-main` label",
      "prov:value": "`.github/workflows/merge-main.yml` is a second CALLER of the same command,\nnever a second resolver (bean `d33q` part B).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean d33q"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "In CI — opt in with the `merge-main` label",
      "prov:value": "It does NOT label the PR: owner\n  ruling 2026-10-03, *\"stop using `needs-merge-human`, it's confusing\n  things\"*, and the measurement behind it is that **a label asserting \"a\n  person is needed\" outlives the condition that set it**. Measured the same\n  day: of ten PRs carrying it, **six were stale** — clean against `main` AND\n  pushable by the bot, because the workflow change that had blocked them was\n  already in their merge-base. A stale hold is indistinguishable from a live\n  one without re-deriving why the push failed, which is the\n  `merge-queue` skill's own §\"A hold has an EXPIRY and a trigger, or it\n  outlives its reason\" at the scale of a whole queue. **The reason lives in the comment, which is dated and names the run; a\n  label is a claim with no timestamp. Measured 2026-10-03 on #1801: the branch ignores `cat-harness/test/results/`\n  while the files stay tracked, git exits 1 when staging an UNMERGED ignored\n  path (it stages it anyway), and merge-main went red on every push to main. Staging a conflicted path uses `git add -f` in both resolvers, safe because\n  the path is one git listed as unmerged. Before #1854 such a\n  run rewrote it to \"**Error** (exit )\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1801",
        "#1854",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-38",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "In CI — opt in with the `merge-main` label",
      "prov:value": "Why it is worth a runner: on #1754 (2026-10-01) one round took 19–46 min in a\nshared agent container while `main` moved every few minutes, and GitHub runs no\n`pull_request` CI on a conflicted PR — a 28-conflict resolution went 'dirty'\nagain within a minute of its push.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1754",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-39",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "When a merge-train member is refused: bean, hand back, or dispatch",
      "prov:value": "The author's side, the queue\nand the bounce-back are the merge-manager SOP in\n[#1802](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/pull/1802) (steps 10 and\n12). The hand-back format is the\n[`agent-handoff`](agent-handoff.md) skill.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1802"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-40",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When a merge-train member is refused: bean, hand back, or dispatch",
      "prov:value": "**Why this exists. Owner, 2026-10-02: *\"if a merge in queue cannot be merged\nfor some reason, create a new bean (under appropriate epic/story…), hand it\nback to the sibling (use the agent-to-agent handoff process with a fail\ncondition) for resolution, or dispatch an agent as appropriate.\"* Before this,\neach refusal got an ad-hoc PR comment or chat message, and nothing in the work\nplan said it had happened. The refusals on 2026-10-02 alone show the three\ncauses this section has to cover:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-41",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Open one bean per refused PR, and check before you create",
      "prov:value": "Only when the PR names no\nbean at all does it go under the steward's own merge-gate epic (`nok9` here),\nand the bean body says so."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-42",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. When no live owner can be reached, dispatch one agent",
      "prov:value": "Two sibling PRs editing one bean\n  (`ob3m`), one script changed differently on both sides (#1822 against\n  #1881), or a page over its budget only in combination (#1764): each of these\n  is a choice between authors.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1822",
        "#1881",
        "#1764"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-43",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. Close the bean when the PR's fate is settled",
      "prov:value": "A refusal bean left open after its PR has gone is\nthe stale state that the `needs-merge-human` label already shows (bean `u7be`\nitem 4).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean u7be"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-conflict-patterns.md#provenance-44",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A merge round — run each check ONCE (owner ruling, 2026-10-05)",
      "prov:value": "**Owner, 2026-10-05, verbatim: *\"trim duplicated steps\"*.** A round of folding\n`main` into a PR was costing about 45 minutes, and most of it was the same\nquestion asked twice. Measured 2026-10-04 on PR #1898's merge rounds, bean\n`7xmc`:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7xmc"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04",
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    }
  ]
